# Notes App - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH (Updated)

# Delete any other spec files. Everything here!

## MASTERPLAN (6 Phases - Execute Sequentially)

### Phase 1: lib/fsNotes.ts (Core FS Layer)

**Interfaces:**

```
interface NoteSummary {
id: string;
slug: string;
title: string;
createdAt: string;
updatedAt: string;
attachmentCount: number
}

interface Note extends NoteSummary {
content: string;
attachments: Attachment[]
}

interface Attachment {
id: string;
originalName: string;
mimeType: string;
size: number;
relativePath: string
}

```

**Functions EXACTLY:**

```
listNotes(): Promise<NoteSummary[]>
getNote(id: string): Promise<Note | null>
createNote(input: {title: string, content: string}): Promise<Note>
updateNote(id: string, input: {title?: string, content?: string}): Promise<Note>
deleteNote(id: string): Promise<void>
listAttachments(noteId: string): Promise<Attachment[]>
saveAttachment(noteId: string, file: File): Promise<Attachment>
deleteAttachment(noteId: string, attId: string): Promise<void>
```

**FS Rules:**

- `NOTES_ROOT/notes/YYYY-MM-DD-slug-uuid/` (e.g. `2026-02-20-projekt-abc123/`)
- Slug: `${date}-${title.toLower().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g,'-')}-${uuid()}`
- `note.md` + `attachments/` folder

### Phase 2: API Routes (app/api/notes/\*\*)

```
app/api/notes/route.ts → GET listNotes(), POST createNote()
app/api/notes/[id]/route.ts → GET/PUT/DELETE
app/api/notes/[id]/attachments/route.ts → GET/POST
app/api/notes/[id]/attachments/[attId]/route.ts → DELETE
```

- NextRequest/NextResponse
- Zod schemas EVERY endpoint
- `{error: string}` responses

### Phase 3: Components

**shadcn/ui components already installed:** button, card, input, dialog, textarea, badge
**Compose custom components using shadcn primitives:**

```
components/MarkdownEditor.tsx ("use client") — uses shadcn Textarea as fallback
components/AttachmentList.tsx — uses shadcn Card, Badge, Button
components/FileUpload.tsx (drag & drop) — uses shadcn Button, Card
components/ThemeToggle.tsx ("use client") — already created, uses shadcn Button + lucide icons
```

- Use shadcn/ui components for all standard UI (Button, Card, Input, Dialog, etc.)
- Compose with Tailwind utilities for layout
- Responsive

### Phase 4: Pages

```
app/notes/page.tsx (list + search) — uses Card for note items, Input for search
app/notes/[id]/page.tsx (edit + upload) — uses Dialog for delete confirm, Button for actions
```

- revalidatePath() after mutations
- Include ThemeToggle in page header/nav

### Phase 5: Docker

```
Dockerfile (multi-stage)
docker-compose.yml (volume ./dev-notes:/app/data)
// use bun instead of npm
```

### Phase 6: Production

```
README Synology deploy
/api/notes/[id]/attachments/[attId]/download endpoint
```

## GLOBAL RULES

- ✅ TypeScript strict
- ✅ No database EVER
- ✅ Tailwind responsive
- ✅ NOTES_ROOT env var
- ✅ ONE FILE PER CMD+K
- ✅ Inline tests EVERY file
- ✅ Commit nach Phase: "Phase X: description"
- ✅ EVERY UI element MUST use the established style system (see STYLE SYSTEM section below)
- ✅ EVERY interactive element (button, input, dialog, etc.) MUST use shadcn/ui from `components/ui/`
- ✅ EVERY color MUST come from CSS variable tokens in `globals.css` — NEVER hardcode hex/rgb/oklch in components
- ✅ Before writing ANY UI code, check `components/ui/` for an existing shadcn component first
- ✅ File naming: PascalCase for components/pages (`NoteEditor.tsx`, `NotesList.tsx`), camelCase for lib/utils (`fsNotes.ts`), lowercase for config (`actions.ts`, `providers.tsx`)
- ✅ **MANDATORY: Run `bun run lint` AND `bunx tsc --noEmit` after EVERY code change AND at the start of every conversation. Fix ALL lint AND type errors before moving on. Zero tolerance — no exceptions, no skipping, no "pre-existing" excuses.**

## BUN RULES

- Use `bun install` instead of `npm i`
- Scripts: `bun --bun next dev`
- Faster installs, native TypeScript

## TESTING PROTOCOL

1. npm run dev
2. curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/notes -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"title":"Test","content":"Hi"}'
3. curl http://localhost:3000/api/notes
4. ls -la dev-notes/notes/
5. Screenshot folder structure

## APPROVED PACKAGES ONLY

```
@uiw/react-md-editor uuid zod gray-matter
shadcn/ui (via CLI: npx shadcn@latest add <component>)
next-themes radix-ui lucide-react
class-variance-authority clsx tailwind-merge tw-animate-css
```

## ABSOLUTE NEVER

- ❌ Database (Prisma, SQLite, etc.)
- ❌ Wrong folder structure
- ❌ UI before complete API
- ❌ Skip phases
- ❌ Experimental Next.js features
- ❌ External CSS frameworks (shadcn/ui is allowed — it's not an external framework, it's copy-paste components)
- ❌ Raw HTML elements when a shadcn/ui component exists (no `<button>`, use `<Button>`)
- ❌ Hardcoded colors (`bg-blue-500`, `text-gray-300`, `#fff`, etc.) — use semantic tokens only
- ❌ `dark:` prefix for themed colors — CSS variables handle light/dark automatically
- ❌ Installing new UI/component libraries without updating this file
- ❌ Custom styling that bypasses the design token system in `globals.css`

## WORKFLOW

Cmd+K: "Phase 1 EXACTLY per .cursorrules"
→ Generate → **Lint & fix ALL errors** → Test → Commit → "Phase 2 ready?"

## STYLE SYSTEM (shadcn/ui + Tailwind v4)

### Architecture
- All colors defined as CSS variables in `app/globals.css` (`:root` for light, `.dark` for dark)
- Registered via `@theme inline` so Tailwind generates utility classes
- Dark/light mode via `next-themes` (class-based, `.dark` on `<html>`)
- ThemeProvider in `app/providers.tsx`, wraps app in `app/layout.tsx`
- Components from shadcn/ui live in `components/ui/`
- `cn()` helper in `lib/utils.ts` for merging Tailwind classes conditionally

### Color Tokens (defined in globals.css)
- `background` / `foreground` — page-level
- `card` / `card-foreground` — cards, panels
- `popover` / `popover-foreground` — dropdowns, tooltips
- `primary` / `primary-foreground` — main actions (buttons, links)
- `secondary` / `secondary-foreground` — secondary actions
- `muted` / `muted-foreground` — subtle backgrounds, placeholder text
- `accent` / `accent-foreground` — hover highlights
- `destructive` / `destructive-foreground` — danger/delete actions
- `border`, `input`, `ring` — borders and focus rings
- `--radius` — global border radius

### Component Rules
- ALWAYS use shadcn/ui components from `components/ui/` for: Button, Card, Input, Dialog, Textarea, Badge
- ALWAYS import with `@/components/ui/...` alias
- ALWAYS use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` to merge conditional classes
- NEVER use raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<dialog>` — use shadcn equivalents
- NEVER hardcode colors (e.g. `bg-blue-500`). ALWAYS use semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`)
- NEVER use `dark:` prefix for themed colors — the CSS variables auto-switch
- To add a new color: add variable in `:root` + `.dark` in `globals.css`, register in `@theme inline`

### Adding New shadcn Components
```
npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>
```

### Installed shadcn Components
button, card, input, dialog, textarea, badge

